["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0cab7-1ed7-77a5-8384-ff10c92e7ad6","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG75a029668365f0f4d270e5cb5f1732237109414c7405ea84759565813acd394b","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/postgres-document-query-parameter","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nThe first live EP fresh-session query against ER 0.17.2 failed before execution because PostgreSQL inferred the containment placeholder as `jsonb` while the provider supplied serialized JSON text. The memory reference tests therefore did not prove the PostgreSQL adapter.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nThe PostgreSQL provider binds its serialized containment predicate as text and casts it to JSONB server-side, and a live provider test selects a nested matching document through the same public query capability EP uses.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe PostgreSQL query now binds the serialized containment document as `text` and performs the JSONB cast in SQL. A provider integration test commits a real document and selects it through `DocumentQueryProvider` against PostgreSQL, closing the adapter gap that memory-only tests missed.\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:the-store-an-adopter-runs-on"},{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Cast serialized containment input through text before PostgreSQL JSONB matching.","title":"PostgreSQL document queries bind JSON text correctly"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG75a029668365f0f4d270e5cb5f1732237109414c7405ea84759565813acd394b","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG75a029668365f0f4d270e5cb5f1732237109414c7405ea84759565813acd394b"]}]